      "text": "Website tựhọc IELTS: https://ielts-fighter.com\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        116.793701171875,
        521.7890014648438,
        154.99375915527344
      ],
      "text": "Before you hear the rest of the talk, you have some time to look at questions 17\nto 20. Now listen and answer questions 17 to 20.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        168.63470458984375,
        496.46136474609375,
        207.23361206054688
      ],
      "text": "OK, now you know some of the things our volunteers do, I’ll go on to some\npractical matters.\n"
    },
    {
      "box": [
        72.0,
        220.2346954345703,
        519.7743530273438,
        656.2736206054688
      ],
      "text": "As you probably know, the town arranges three major festivals every year, and\nthey all depend on a large number of volunteers. The book festival lasts three\ndays, and uses several venues which all need volunteers. More are needed for\nthe music festival because that lasts a whole week, and even more help is\nrequired for the science festival, even though it's only two days long. It\ninvolves quite a lot of venues, though. It’s a good idea to help at the festival\nyou’re most interested in, because you can attend most of the events for free.\nWe try to use volunteers who are flexible, though, because some festival\nevents are held outdoors and the weather may affect the size of the audience\nand even whether the event can take place so there can be changes at short\nnotice. What’s essential though is being able to get on well with other people\nand also to deal with someone who's behaving badly, as occasionally happens.\nOur plan is to get you all working in September, after a week’s training starting\non the 2nd, so we’ll be timetabling you for duties the following week from the\n9th onward. Later in the week beginning September 23rd we have a chat with\neach of you to find out how you feel about being a volunteer and what extra\nsupport you need. As a thank you to the volunteers we arrange an annual\nevent. In recent years we’ve had a party in the Town Hall and last year a\nbarbecue in Chamber Park. Our forthcoming event is a trip along the canal\nfrom here to Dewhurst and back. It's on Saturday, September the 28th. And if\nyou'd like to attend, you can sign up once you start work. Now, this is the\nVolunteer's T-shirt.\n"
    }
  ]
